etter! Where's my multi-fucking-billions of dollars?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T16:30:38-07:00","id":190870,"title":"","content":"I think you need an agent to talk to Disney.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T17:51:40-07:00","id":190974,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing: <i>everyone has written a better prequel trilogy by now</i>.<br /> <br /> I don't say that derisively, it's just, well, almost ten years after the fact. So...it is a fact. Hell, I wrote a outline much like this one a while back(although P. Bear, you have a lot of nice touches I didn't, namely the visions).<br /> <br /> And on a minor note, the ability to write a better prequel trilogy doesn't create talent for the VII-IX movies-especially considering how many people still work off of a broken down version of Lucas's version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T06:58:15-07:00","id":191352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=190974#post190974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing: <i>everyone has written a better prequel trilogy by now</i>.<br /> <br /> I don't say that derisively, it's just, well, almost ten years after the fact. So...it is a fact. Hell, I wrote a outline much like this one a while back(although P. Bear, you have a lot of nice touches I didn't, namely the visions).<br /> <br /> And on a minor note, the ability to write a better prequel trilogy doesn't create talent for the VII-IX movies-especially considering how many people still work off of a broken down version of Lucas's version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, everybody has had time to think about it and hindsight is 20/20, etc, etc, etc........but really, what this shows is that George Lucas needs a good editor and someone who isn't an Ascended Fan-Boy who will tell him it's all brilliant.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I love these movies, even the bad ones I consider better than a lot of the other crap available in the mass media, but even I would have told him, &quot;No, George, Jar-Jar is a bad idea. And Padme dying of a broken heart or whatever....uh uh. And ditch that midichlorian shit! Magic doesn't need a sci-fi explanation. Save that shit for Star <b>TREK</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Besides, while some of this has been rattling around in my head for a while, it only came into focus about a week or so ago, and I typed up that post in-between taking calls at my work yesterday. Lucas had 20+ years to get that shit together and that WAS his job!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T07:08:21-07:00","id":191355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=191352#post191352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic doesn't need a sci-fi explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially when the explanation is a fact devoid of context that therefore doesn't answer any questions and raises more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T07:21:18-07:00","id":191361,"title":"","content":"Don't need no midichlorians. Just need the Force to be with me.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://images.amcnetworks.com/blogs.amctv.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/ForceUnleashed_560x330.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T07:23:58-07:00","id":191364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=191355#post191355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially when the explanation is a fact devoid of context that therefore doesn't answer any questions and raises more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I didn't even dignify it by calling it a scientific explanation. He didn't just pull that out of his ass, he pulled it out of a Wampa's ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T09:22:20-07:00","id":191457,"title":"","content":"Wampa ass cheese.<br /> <br /> Don't think on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T12:03:22-07:00","id":199139,"title":"","content":"New topic: Disney is cheating!!!!!!!!!!!<br /> <br /> My Baby Bears, being little girls, are like so many of their peers (and way older females) enamored with the latest Disney princess movie, <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt2294629/\" target=\"_blank\">Frozen</a>. If you haven't seen it, stop now because I will not be hiding the spoilers. If you have, you might want to watch it again after this. Because of how often they insist on watching this, my brain has had time to analyze this movie even without my conscious effort. As such, I have found something sinister out about the whole thing.<br /> <br /> Okay, I lied, here's the spoiler tag, but it won't be safe after this.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Why has Disney cheated? Because they have spent decades enforcing and encouraging some tropes so much they are the trope codifier for most of them. And now they make this movie, <i>break several of their most important ones</i>, and get one of the biggest animated films ever! <b>NO FAIR! </b>You should not get to break your own formula and do <b><i>better</i></b>!!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0093779/quotes\" target=\"_blank\">Lemme esplain......there is no time, lemme sum-up:</a><br /> <br /> <u>Older Woman with (usually magic) power over the princess is always the villain.</u><br /> Snow White has the Wicked Queen<br /> Cinderella her her Step-Mother<br /> Aurora (Sleeping Beauty) has Malifecent<br /> Ariel (Little Mermaid) has Ursala<br /> Rapunzel (Tangled) has Mother Gothel<br /> <b>Frozen </b>has Queen Elsa. The big sister who's really just scared and as much a victim as the princess (Anna) and hasn't really done anything bad to her besides following the (poor) instructions of their parents.<br /> <br /> <u>Princess sees the Prince and falls in love at first sight.</u><br /> Snow White, Cinderella, Aurora and Ariel are all guilty of this one.<br /> <b>Frozen </b>has Anna falling in love with her Prince Hans......only it turns out he's a complete psychopath and never loved her and was going to manipulate and potentially murder her to get the throne for himself.<br /> <br /> <u>The only way the princess is going to get away from all this is by running off with the Prince.</u><br /> Same guilty parties as above, plus Rapunzel.<br /> <b>Frozen</b>.....see above, her prince was gonna be the one to put her in a miserable situation in the first place.<br /> <br /> <u>The funny little friends who help the princess achieve her goals and keep her safe are never human.</u><br /> Snow White have dwarves, nearly all the rest had (semi) intelligent animals.<br /> Belle had animated furniture and knick-knacks.<br /> <b>Frozen </b>has the first human ever, Kristoff, and he's the one who actually gets the princess instead of the prince!<br /> <br /> <u>Said funny little friends are never a threat to the Prince.</u><br /> See above, dude got the girl.<br /> <br /> Seriously, go watch that movie and see for yourself. I've probably missed a few here, but it's like they took the entire Disney Princess formula that they created, twisted it 180, and <i>made a better movie for it!!!</i> Sneaky, lucky bastards!!!<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Friggin' Disney......bought up my damn childhood, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T13:28:46-07:00","id":199203,"title":"","content":"It was all in the plans from the beginning. People like the unexpected, so you spend decades establishing tropes as being THE ONLY POSSIBLE WAY THINGS CAN HAPPEN and then you make a movie breaking several of them and have your biggest hit ever.<br /> <br /> Clever, Disney. Clever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T10:49:51-07:00","id":220332,"title":"","content":"My 2 year old is going to be a hacker: Another topic to avoid talking about something else...........<br /> <br /> So far, my 2 year old (Little Baby Bear) has managed to open an iPhone and a Nook and dial her aunt on a non-smart phone. Now, this may not sound impressive, but there's more to it.<br /> <br /> For the iPhone, it belongs to her uncle and he had a 4 digit code on it that had to be used to unlock it, then it could be swiped on the screen to open it. She figured out the code, swiped the screen to open it, got to the Contacts list and was dialing his work for him.<br /> <br /> For Papa Bear's Nook, it requires a few steps to open it. It has a cover (that has to be flipped open), press the power button on the side (instead of the volume buttons on the opposite side), slide the correct icon from the outer edges of a circle on the screen to the exact center in a space about the size of a nickel, and then it's unlocked. Not only did she do all this, including correctly choosing the icon to open the Baby Bears books instead of mine, she had opened the Library, found the book she wanted, and it was 90% loaded before I came back into the room. I left to get something to drink from the fridge, the entire trip look less than a minute.<br /> <br /> For Grandma's phone, it's a flip phone (this is Mama Bear's mother, who is not very tech savvy at all), not a smart phone. That means there's no sliding, but she had to open it and push buttons. She either pressed the right button (and held it) to activate the speed dial function to reach her aunt OR she somehow got it to dial the last number dialed....which would have also required pressing several buttons and/or scrolling thru a list of options.<br /> <br /> <br /> Last thing, just for emphasis.............SHE TURNED <b>2, T-W-O, </b>IN MARCH OF THIS YEAR!!!!!<br /> <br /> I have a feeling that Big Baby Bear will be the one who makes me go into her school to talk to the principal because she's mouthing off, but Little Baby Bear will be the one who causes the CIA to show up at our door because she's been playing Global Thermonuclear War with the NORAD computers....................again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T11:11:50-07:00","id":220350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=220332#post220332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a feeling that Big Baby Bear will be the one who makes me go into her school to talk to the principal because she's mouthing off, but Little Baby Bear will be the one who causes the CIA to show up at our door because she's been playing Global Thermonuclear War with the NORAD computers....................again.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be silly! There's no way that would happen.<br /> <br /> it would be the FBI that does that. Probably with a SWAT team or five.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T11:45:03-07:00","id":220372,"title":"","content":"And then I had a mental image of Papa Bear never posting here again because he and his family just vanish one night, and their youngest is kidnapped to be raised in a brainwashing government installation to grow into America's premiere information-control agent. Of course all her best work is done on computers on account of her being a bad spy since everyone notices the polar bear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T11:51:25-07:00","id":220374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=220372#post220372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course all her best work is done on computers on account of her being a bad spy since everyone notices the polar bear.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, dammit, Russia isn't one of our enemies, because a polar bear would be less noticeable there..................................and no, that's not where I spent the 1980s and you can't prove otherwise.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T10:27:25-07:00","id":248959,"title":"","content":"Today's thought: Am I the only one who played in groups that seemed to pay attention to the Golden Rule of White Wolf, often paraphrased by said groups as &quot;so long as it makes it a better game, fuck the rules!&quot;?<br /> <br /> There have, of course, been numerous posts about this and several other posts supporting the idea and talking about the games in which it doesn't happen. But here's my thing about it........<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion/page19\">First, this is after having read a post in the Forsaken forums about the Idigam Chronicles development and how they're trying to work into the book a way for the pack's totem to be raised not just by experience points, but by things that actually happen in the story.</a> Now, the actual details of this don't matter as much to me as the fact that there seems to be a need to <b>write this shit into the book.</b> Really? People don't feel comfortable just saying to their group &quot;Hey, your characters just did something seriously kick-ass! You're all gonna get this cool thing because <i><b>that's how the story played out</b></i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Second thing, all these Beats and Conditions and such seem like they're ways for putting mechanics on shit we already did all the time, anyway. So, again, people really need this spelled out in the books? Did I just happen to get some really great players and STs to learn from, or is everyone else waiting for the WW/CCP/OP police ninjas to swoop down on them to tell them that it's <b>BAD WRONG FUN!!!</b> Did these players get grief about &quot;their way&quot; being <b>BAD WRONG FUN</b> from so many sources they actually believed it? I've been playing these games (shit, lemme think.....1994, maybe 1995 or so.....fucking hell 20 years, shit I'm old!) for a while......and I've never had those ninjas show up AND everything I always read encouraged us to play the game to make it fun, and if that meant bending, breaking, bedding, or abusing the rules <b>SO BE IT!</b><br /> <br /> And now in a very obvious burying of the lead, this is one of those moments when I feel like the whole game and systems are leaving me behind because I don't get what the purpose of some of this stuff is and so many other seems to be so excited by it. Hunter, Geist, Mummy and Demon seem to get so much (nearly fanatic) appreciation for things that I don't get from them. People seem to love the Tier system, and I look at it and say, &quot;um, yeah, didn't we just get away from those global conspiracies in the Classic WOD?&quot; The Krewes seem to be nothing more than an elaborate system for making the player group. There's supposed to be a deep, horrific mystery in Mummy that I simply cannot find. What little I've read of Demon has not grabbed my attention. My recent acquisition of Masquerade 20 and Apocalypse 20 have just kicked me harder in the ass with nostalgia and I'm regressing back in anticipation of Ascension 20. I still don't have enough time to take for a game, and I know it's my choice because I'm putting my Baby Bears first, but it's still depressing.<br /> <br /> tl:dr - &quot;My games&quot;, though I know I have no right to call them that, are moving beyond me and I'm sad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T10:39:18-07:00","id":248965,"title":"","content":"Most players don't enjoy that sort of stuff, and thus it needs incentives for those folks. I think it's kind of clever in that aspect. I know I've had players who would never willingly plan on losing Morality/Integrity, let alone losing a leg.<br /> <br /> EDIT: In fact, a lot of players need help deciding to do the wrong thing as a player, because no one wants to do the wrong thing-it feels like losing to most people's mindsets.<br /> <br /> As for Hunter, Geist, Mummy, and Demon, well...Mummy's a niche game. THere's a lot to Iike about it, even though it <i>is</i> lacking in that big mystery so far(A mystery that I feel like they're taking the whole of the series to tell, rather than covering in the original Storyteller's section), but it's niche.<br /> <br /> I ran Hunter and vastly enjoyed it, Geist was and might still be third favorite(although I expect Idigam to claim that, if it doesn't also knock Demon down a peg), and Demon became my second. So if you want to chat and get some additional perspective, I'm available.<br /> <br /> Still, not all games are going to be for all people. It happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-04-2014, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T11:44:23-07:00","id":249025,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's just me, then. I've let characters of mine <b>die </b>because it's how their luck played out. Even when the ST has given me an out, I did it anyway. One had been a <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/KarmaHoudini\" target=\"_blank\">Karmic Houdini</a> for years and dumb luck finally slammed his sorry ass into the ground and said, &quot;Nope, this time you die, and in a totally undignified way, by falling into a trap even the big, dumb, lumbering Brujah avoided.&quot;<br /> <br /> And I know you're there to pick your brain, Arc buddy, but for some reason, it's just not sticking. You'd think that arcane espionage would appeal to a <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> junkie, since that is a totally valid way to play that game, but it's just not clicking. And it's not just that not all games are not for all people, the last game I was excited about was <b>Changeling: the Lost</b>, which was just starting to be talked about when the last game I was running ended. I'm sure it's not coincidence. I was still an active ST at the time, so I was much more involved and invested in everything. Now, it's all abstract information since it's not something I'm <i>doing</i>, just reading about.<br /> <br /> Maybe some day, I'll be able to get back in more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T14:32:48-07:00","id":253592,"title":"","content":"Fukkity, fuck, fuck, fuck!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! Hate my job, hate my boss who is a completely fucking moron, and I've come to the realization I cannot speak to ANY co-workers about it because they take everything I say and do back to her and it's automatically placed in the worst possible light!!!!!!!!!!!<br /> <br /> Just had to get that out of my system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov