/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=255284#post255284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, following up on that, now filing a grievance against my boss. One of the advantages to being in a union: you can actually tell your boss when they're wrong and not get fired.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything happened on this front?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T08:33:15-07:00","id":269115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=269067#post269067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything happened on this front?</div> </div> </div> </div>Meeting for it is later today. Check back again in about 3 hours.<br /> <br /> EDIT FOR UPDATE:<br /> Didn't go as well as I hoped, but it was a step. Basically, boss lied her ass off and laid it all at my feet as the problem for not communicating the issues around here better (which I have communicated, she just ignores them) and letting it get to me personally (and how am I supposed to react when other people get listened to, and I'm not?). BUT, she has to respond with a &quot;remedy plan&quot;, which documents what she agrees to do about it from here forward and if she doesn't adhere to that, further action can be taken. While I didn't expect her to be dismissed on the spot, of course, it still fell short of expectations.<br /> <br /> But hey, it's only the second time I ever complained against a boss and didn't get fired! So, bonus there!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 09-30-2014, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T14:56:00-07:00","id":271124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For lack of a better title, and based on what's established, it would have to be something like &quot;Wraith: the Remembering/Fading/Anchored&quot;, I think.<br /> <br /> A post-survival horror game.<br /> <br /> Similar to Mummy in that there would be a serious focus on remembering who you are (were?), why you continue on and what you have to do to keep going.<br /> <br /> Underworld geography would remain the same, but the Wraiths (like Geists and Kerberoi) would have special advantages for their unique state.<br /> <br /> Some of the things that would make them different from the other ghosts is that they have not tied themselves to a single Dominion, they are not anchorless, and their powers are based around using/applying memories they have from their previous life. For example, if they want to cross one of the Rivers, they don't just dive in, they remember themselves going on a long trip. This allows for adding new powers as they manage to dig out more memories from their souls. That's another thing, it's not just a reflection of what they once were, it's their actual soul and thoughts and memories wrapped up into an ectoplasmic form. What they risk, daily, is losing all that, which would be measured by the Morality/Integrity stat. Their anchors would be much more important as they'd be a place to replenish memories and gain new ones. Interacting with the living world would also help build those things up, but it brings with it the risk of running into mages, sin-eaters, kerberoi, etc, etc, etc that can mess with ghosts. As a default, and to show their stronger connection to the living world, they would all have Manifest as an automatic, built-in Numina.<br /> <br /> And my short burst of creativity has ended for now. </div> </div> </div>Importing this over here so I don't take over the thread it came from. Just latched on to this idea: Wraith: the Post-Survival Horror game<br /> <br /> Expanding on above:<br /> <br /> While the living world has it's fair share of perils, Wraiths are not safe in the Underworld, either. Generally, the ghosts and the Kerberoi will leave a Wraith to his deathly existence, unless the Wraith does something to draw a lot of attention to himself. The ghosts will take notice. They could be curious about why he can do what they can't and they will react to that knowledge in various ways. They will ask, they will insist and when further denied, they will demand. They will claw, weep, tear and rage at the Wraith to get it if they feel like it. Other could just clamor all over the Wraith in great numbers like a Deathlands Messiah, looking for a miracle to get them out of their awful state. If all of this disrupts the Dominion sufficiently, the Wraith could find himself with a Kerberoi on his ephemeral ass. Driven out, carried out, thrown in prison, etc, etc....whatever they decide is the appropriate punishment for being too alive in the lands of the dead.<br /> <br /> I'll keep coming back to this.<br /> <br /> EDIT: A little more.<br /> <br /> No matter how much the plead, beg, bribe or demand, there is no way for a Wraith to make a ghost into something like itself. Once a ghost has lost enough of itself, there is no going back. This is one of the threats a Wraith deals with daily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 10-02-2014, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T08:17:20-07:00","id":274730,"title":"","content":"<b>Okay, that is it!</b><br /> <br /> This year, I've had to put my wife's dog down, my grandmother (who helped raise me as my mother was one of the early single mothers of the 1970s) has died, my wife's uncle died about a month ago and NOW her father died in an UGLY way this Friday!<br /> <br /> No more deaths of anyone I know, GOT IT!?!?<br /> <br /> You depressed folks on here, that means you too!<br /> <br /> The Grim Reaper is staying out of my circle of friends &amp; family for at least 5 years! ((I'd say longer, but I know what kind of health conditions my parents and mother-in-law have))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T09:06:16-07:00","id":274766,"title":"","content":"I'll try to avoid dying for the time being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T09:21:47-07:00","id":274780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=274766#post274766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll try to avoid dying for the time being.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd better, or I'll kick your ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T10:51:09-07:00","id":274851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=274730#post274730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NOW her father died in an UGLY way this Friday!</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything you want to talk about?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=274730#post274730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No more deaths of anyone I know, GOT IT!?!?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well shit, I guess that means I gotta change my plans for Saturday. And figure out some plans for Sunday. Eh, maybe I'll go out to that burger place I like.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T11:40:41-07:00","id":274893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=274851#post274851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything you want to talk about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. I've had to hear my wife go one about her portion of it, so I'm kinda sick and tired of it. At the same time, I think I need to put it out there just to get it out of my system.<br /> <br /> Spoiled for the squeamish....which includes me.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Grandpa was hospitalized about 3 weeks prior to all this, got out on a Friday and was set up with hospice at our home that day, with his hospital bed right there in the family room (BTW, why is it called this? My family stays in the living room....which is now ironic since someone died in the other room, maybe we should make it the dying room and the living room.....anyway) next to the door out to the garage, so he wasn't exactly any place that could be hidden. He went from no pain meds to a good dose within a week since his kidneys were shutting down. All this went down this Friday. Friday mornings, both Baby Bears go to daycare to give their Grandma a day without anyone to worry about but Grandpa. That is the one good thing out of all this. We already had them dressed and ready to go and kept in the living room to have a little breakfast before going. I'm running things out to the car when I see something dark all across the bottom of his face and chest. Upon closer inspection, I see that he's thrown up over night and he didn't have the strength/desire to roll over or do anything about it. His last meal was chocolate cake, so it's a lovely dark brown, which is probably mixed with bile, just to make it extra nasty. He's still gurgling, so I don't know if he's lost enough oxygen at this point for his brain to shut down and his body to keep going or if he can be saved at all. As quickly as I can, I rush everything out to the car, make sure the lights stay off, tell Mama Bear (his daughter) that she'll need to check on him as soon as we're out the door. I keep the Baby Bears moving quickly thru the door and out, but I get to leave my wife and her mother to deal with him and get to see him like that. Later on, I find out that he jerked and twitched and gargled some more and opened his eyes and looked at them, traumatizing his wife and daughter.<br /> <br /> I spent some time yelling at that asshole the other night. HE decided to go on hospice and give up. HE decides to not try anymore and didn't make any attempt to save himself. HE gets to check out and leave a LITERAL mess for his wife and daughter to clean up so that HE doesn't have to deal with it any more. Selfish fucker.<br /> <br /> At least I got my girls out of there and away from it before it traumatized them, too. But the Eldest Baby Bear is old enough to understand he's not coming back. Littlest Baby Bear just keeps telling us we need to go pick him up from wherever he's at, which she can't decide where he is.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> And that's how I spent my Friday.<br /> <br /> Everybody else have fun?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":