ions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T12:11:12-08:00","id":311503,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's why I mentioned it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T07:15:45-08:00","id":316232,"title":"","content":"WHOO-HOO! I hit 300 Likes!<br /> <br /> What?<br /> <br /> Just taking my positives where I can get them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T15:10:04-08:00","id":383638,"title":"","content":"K, need help from my French hommes (and femmes):<br /> <br /> Stumbled across this very nice album called <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/The-Rough-Guide-Paris-Lounge/dp/B004NTVM38\" target=\"_blank\">The Rough Guide to Paris Lounge</a>. There's one artist in particular who's caught my attention, <a href=\"http://www.feloche.fr/Biographie\" target=\"_blank\">Feloche</a>. For all I know, he's the French version of Justin Bieber, but I like his sound.<br /> <br /> I need a little assistance on a few things.<br /> <br /> 1) Does anyone else know him/listen to him?<br /> 2) Where does he sit in the French music scene? Mainstream? Popular? Obscure? Alternative? Did I just find the French version of Bieber, Beck, the Beatles or Beethoven?<br /> 3) This is the demanding one - can someone please translate the lyrics to the song <b>Bon appetit shaman</b>? I know what bon appetit (good appetite/eating) means and I know what a shaman is (in English, anyway, does it mean something else in French), but without knowing what the rest of the lyrics mean, it makes it just a very odd reference. I'm trying to figure out if it's more than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T16:28:16-08:00","id":383780,"title":"","content":"Hi, French guy here.<br /> <br /> So... I absolutely never heard of this guy. He sure doesn't sound like the French Justin Bieber (I don't even think we have an equivalent for him, thank god). Apparently, he's pretty obscure, so, congrats for finding him, I guess!<br /> <br /> About 3) : shaman means exactly the same in french, except that we usually spell it chaman. I can't find the lyrics to the song, so I can't translate it for you, but the title alone doesn't really make a reference to anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T07:33:03-08:00","id":384201,"title":"","content":"Hmm, so it looks like I stumbled across a new guy (kinda figured with just 2 albums, but you never know). Cool.<br /> <br /> There's a couple of other artists on this album this I have to ask about<b></b>:<br /> <a href=\"http://www.pascalparisot.com/category/news/\" target=\"_blank\">Pascal Parisot</a> - I found 3 albums for him, so maybe he's getting his name out there.<br /> Caravan Palace - an electro swing band.....that alone makes things interesting, having trouble loading their web-site.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anything? Other obscure artists? Did I find the hipster album? Did I stumble across the audio equivalent of a tourist trap?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm always trying to get a sense of where these things land in the culture they come from. An artist doesn't exist in a vacuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T07:44:15-08:00","id":384204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=302134#post302134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever started to do something you've done 1,000 times before, something you're quite confident about in your abilities to perform, something that's very vital to your person or character or well being.........................and you couldn't do it? You did everything the way you were supposed to and nothing happened.<br /> <br /> Halloween night, that happened to me. I've never hid the fact that my mystical/spiritual/psychological beliefs are anything but &quot;not mainstream&quot;. I talk to the street light to make then turn green. I threaten my computer to scare the gremlins inside. Last Halloween I had a visit from my great-grandmother and my grandfather and had a conversation with my totem (a bear of course, not a polar bear though). Earlier this year, I lost my grandmother, so I was hoping to get a visit from her.<br /> <br /> And what I got was nothing.<br /> <br /> I was out there completely alone.<br /> <br /> Nothing and no one came to visit.<br /> <br /> I don't even know what to do about it.<br /> <br /> I don't know how much of this is from the little asshole who lives in my head, but I keep thinking that I just need to walk away from all of it. The problem there is that these things, these beliefs, <b>these practices are what has kept me away from the psychiatrist and the heavy medications they want to put me on.<br /> <br /> I don't want to go on their drugs. </b>I can't talk to the spirits anymore. I am at an impasse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, how's your day?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'm quoting myself, fuck off.<br /> <br /> See that part I highlighted above?<br /> <br /> Guess where I'm going next Tuesday?<br /> <br /> Yup, to get drugs.<br /> <br /> I'm trying hard to not think of this as a defeat because I know I've crossed the line where everything else I've done for years can help anymore. I'm conceding a single battle to the little asshole in my head, but if I'm still here, then the war is not over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T08:21:33-08:00","id":384241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=384201#post384201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, so it looks like I stumbled across a new guy (kinda figured with just 2 albums, but you never know). Cool.<br /> <br /> There's a couple of other artists on this album this I have to ask about<b></b>:<br /> <a href=\"http://www.pascalparisot.com/category/news/\" target=\"_blank\">Pascal Parisot</a> - I found 3 albums for him, so maybe he's getting his name out there.<br /> Caravan Palace - an electro swing band.....that alone makes things interesting, having trouble loading their web-site.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anything? Other obscure artists? Did I find the hipster album? Did I stumble across the audio equivalent of a tourist trap?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm always trying to get a sense of where these things land in the culture they come from. An artist doesn't exist in a vacuum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Never heard of Pascal Parisot either. A quick research taught me that he's actually a children's singer, so no, he's not really famous here.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Caravan Palace? They're downright amazing. I've seen them live, best concert I've ever been. They're not exactly <i>that</i> mainstream, but they are known : they made a few appearances on tv, they did a tour in the US, they got an award for their first album... <br /> <br /> (And for your last post : ouch. I don't know your backstory, so I can't offer advice and I won't, since it seems that you mostly need to rant. Still : I'm sorry for what's happening to you.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T09:46:39-08:00","id":384295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=384204#post384204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying hard to not think of this as a defeat because I know I've crossed the line where everything else I've done for years can help anymore. I'm conceding a single battle to the little asshole in my head, but if I'm still here, then the war is not over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking medicine when sick is not shameful. It is, as best I understand the term, respectful of one's health, and I'm glad you're getting help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T10:16:07-08:00","id":384311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div