"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I discovered the last time I looked into it (when we were discussing the star wars lightsaber trailer) while the forum has a system for images it has been deliberately disabled.<br /> <br /> So linking it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bugger, ah well, such is the life of a bear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T08:06:48-07:00","id":462258,"title":"","content":"Rassin' frakin' rumblin' grumblin'.............yes, I swear like a monster from Legend of Zelda when frustrated enough to post but not enough to be genuinely upset.<br /> <br /> <br /> First of all, since I'm not playing any games, I'm totally unmotivated to read any of the new releases from OP/WW.<br /> <br /> Second, because I'm still looking for something to read, I can't think of anything good and I have no new Dresden Files to go thru.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I did have a positive here. In working on rebuilding my spiritual/intuitive thinking, I found a new totem thanks to a friend. Someone pointed out my bear claw plate looked like rain/thunder/lightning clouds from upside down. So, now I have Storm Bear....not sure what that means yet, but the storms and I have always had a bit of a connection, so I'm wanting to explore that one. I've walked home in tornadoes and not been hurt. I've been outside, unprotected, in hurricane-like conditions and not even caught a cold. I've driven in horrible hail storms and got my whole family home in one piece when others were pulling over to wait it out. I've been lucky, and maybe a bit more. I know it's all crazy, but it helps my mind knit itself back together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T06:49:17-07:00","id":472657,"title":"","content":"Just a spot of wisdom today......or spotty wisdom, whatever it might be.....<br /> <br /> We all have jobs, but that doesn't mean we <b>are </b>our jobs. Something that is defined by it's function and usefulness is not a person, but a tool. A couch is a couch because of it's couchness. You can sit on it or lay on it comfortably and as soon as it's failed in that purpose, it's discarded and replaced.<br /> <br /> So, today's thought, don't be a tool. Be a person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T11:13:52-07:00","id":473075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=472657#post472657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a spot of wisdom today......or spotty wisdom, whatever it might be.....<br /> <br /> We all have jobs, but that doesn't mean we <b>are </b>our jobs. Something that is defined by it's function and usefulness is not a person, but a tool. A couch is a couch because of it's couchness. You can sit on it or lay on it comfortably and as soon as it's failed in that purpose, it's discarded and replaced.<br /> <br /> So, today's thought, don't be a tool. Be a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>That hit home. Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T11:21:36-07:00","id":473086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=473075#post473075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That hit home. Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome. I might make this a regular thing as I have all sorts of odd thoughts during my long drive to and from work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T11:49:05-07:00","id":473113,"title":"","content":"Do I have Morality or Clarity?<br /> <br /> If I get lost in my own head too much, is that a loss of Clarity?<br /> <br /> If I have trouble separating my imagination from the world around me, is that a slip of Clarity?<br /> <br /> Is the fact that I am writing this one, too?<br /> <br /> Or am I just really freakin' tired?<br /> <br /> Who knows....maybe tomorrow, I'll figure it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T07:32:13-07:00","id":474284,"title":"","content":"Today's thought is more observational.<br /> <br /> I was feeling very cosmopolitan this morning in the very strict dictionary definition of the word.<br /> <br /> I was wearing a jacket from Cabo San Lucas (made in Mexico), drinking Gevalia (Swedish coffee), eating a croissant (French pastry) in a Pontiac (American car company named after an Ottawa chieftain).<br /> <br /> Only in America, as they say, whomever &quot;they&quot; are.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:28:44-07:00","id":474844,"title":"","content":"If I am he as you are he as you are me and we are all together..................who are &quot;they&quot;?","signature":"<hr clas