the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T17:54:10-07:00","id":506281,"title":"","content":"So, myself. On the Seeming Front, I think there's decent arguments for Darkling or Fairest, maybe some smaller ones for Beast or Ogre. I sincerely hope I'm not a Wizened, but I'll concede possible arguments exist there as well.<br /> <br /> On the Kith front, Author is valid, as is Shadowsoul if you go Fairest(that weird balance of reclusive and loud). Some people'd probably accuse me of being a Fireheart, though I suspect them of confusing fire with water, if elemental characterization is a thing we go with. There's a decent argument for Coyote or Troll. If I had any actual musical talent a Nightsinger would have come up, but Palewraith or Moonborn are possibles. Razorhand, not as much these days-I'm capable of violence, but nowhere near as violent as I used to be. Gameplayer's also possible.<br /> <br /> THat's what you get. I'm a little too dynamic to easily categorize, in my own mind-but in reality I'm simpler than I imagine, so I'll let y'all make your own calls.<br /> <br /> It doesn't help I'm in the middle of information juggling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T08:02:08-07:00","id":506793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=506258#post506258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I considered Wizened.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I offer you two options.<br /> <br /> Option 1: the Durance I imagined for you here based on your answers.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Keeper in question needed a librarian. Someone to keep the books of lore and fables and myths and stories all in order. You seemed to have a knack for it and a love of books, so he took you. 10 years of drudging around the books, keeping them together as best you could. Problem was, there was no cart, no central desk to leave them out. They were scattered about the castle of this Gentry, so you're schlepping the books from one end of the place to another all day long. One of the few advantages is that your Keeper didn't care how <i>quickly </i>they got put back, just as long as they were in <i>order</i>. So, you'd take a break and read the books. It was all the secrets of the Fae and their ways in story forms. You learned and grew in knowledge, and in this place, that meant extraordinary power. One day, you realized you could see the way out the castle, thru the Hedge and back home in your mind as if it was playing on a movie screen. So, you walked right out and your Keeper never even noticed until you were long gone. After your return, you noticed that you continued to have a knack for being able to see things as they played out well in advance of the actual events. It's like your mind had the advanced previews of the whole world. You've become a Wizened Oracle renowned for your accuracy.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Option 2: the tie-breaker questions, which require even more personal insight.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[