ar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T10:08:26-07:00","id":510860,"title":"","content":"I mean does anyone have good dreams.<br /> <br /> Although I suppose that <i>does</i> count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T10:29:39-07:00","id":510874,"title":"","content":"A few weeks ago, I dreamed of the zombie apocalypse. Except with a twist : during the day, they reverted to normal people.<br /> <br /> Which actually caused a lot of new problems : the uninfected had even more trouble killing zombies since the police would be after them, they had to sleep during the day, and most of them had trouble keeping their jobs because of this! PROBLEMS, I TELL YOU.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T10:37:41-07:00","id":510881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=510858#post510858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Congratulations P. Bear. You have become the online quiz of Onyx Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind as long as no one gets impatient with me. My methods take time. If it gets bad enough, I'll start telling people the reasons for those 4 questions and let people self-diagnose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T11:15:34-07:00","id":510899,"title":"","content":"Still working on Arc's second one, here's Jeddy's.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Like so many of these stories, they begin with you taking a wrong turn. You stepped thru the wrong archway while out for a walk. The ground started to get muddier, the sounds shifted to what seemed to be a river or stream flowing briskly. As you finally found the stream, you noticed it was quite still. The sound was a dual line of swordsman on the other side, clashing their swords together high above in an arch. Behind and above them was an extraordinary large figure, face obscured under a large and wide helmet of sorts. He beckons you forward thru the archway of swords and you move carefully thru, ducking beneath their blows as best you can. The Keeper makes a simple offer: Pledge yourself to me, tend to my men\u2019s wounds, and you will leave here with skills that will dazzle the most skilled healer. Give me 10 years and I will give you a lifetime of adoration. You look it with abandon and saw war and death and wounds and poisons and disease and every method of madness that could harm the body and a few you never imagined could be true. 10 years turned to 20. The work was too good, too tempting. Every time you thought you could leave, the men would beg you to stay and present you a new battalion of wounds to heal. 20 years turned into 30 and they never ran out of wounded, and that\u2019s when you realized that was the game. They never would run out. They would never let you go until you were too bent and broken to serve them anymore. In the dead of night, you finally saw an opportunity. Another wound needing a rare herb. You went out to get it yourself, and just kept walking. Eventually, you found the river, noticing this time, from this side, it was a river of blood. Weary, fingers numb, back aching, knees weak, feet sore, you kept walking. On the other side, you found the way back thru the mud and the trees and the bushes. On the other side was a friend you hadn\u2019t seen in 30 years looking exactly the same. \u201cWhat took you so long? I\u2019ve been waiting here for HOURS! Let\u2019s go.\u201d Outside, you look the same, if a bit tired looking. Inside and to the other Changelings, they see the Wizened Brewer/Chirurgeon left behind. You\u2019d be a better Chirurgeon if not for the damage done to your body, it\u2019s just too hard for your fingers to work that well or to stay on your feet for that long.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T12:21:24-07:00","id":511029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=510826#post510826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gimme what you got there, I'll see if I can work with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Better idea - if you don't know about Changeling, instead of which Seeming &amp; Kith, tell which which of these scares you more:<br /> Fear of the unknown<br /> Fear of turning into a monster<br /> Fear of giving into instincts and losing yourself<br /> Fear of living up to standards you can't meet<br /> Fear of being left behind<br /> Fear of being overwhelmed by something bigger than yourself","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T13:20:58-07:00","id":511069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=511029#post511029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Better idea - if you don't know about Changeling, instead of which Seeming &amp; Kith, tell which which of these scares you more:<br /> Fear of the unknown<br /> Fear of turning into a monster<br /> Fear of giving into instincts and losing yourself<br /> Fear of living up to standards you can't meet<br /> Fear of being left behind<br /> Fear of being overwhelmed by something bigger than yourself</div> </div> </div> </div>Not aimed at me, but I have definite stress and fear about living up to standards I can't meet and being overwhelmed by things bigger than me. You've seen my freakouts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T13:29:53-07:00","id":511074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=510860#post510860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean does anyone have good dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the majority of my dreams are bad, I do remember my dreams pretty much every day, and that leads to a fair number of good dreams. Last night, I dreamed about hanging out with my sister and her kids. Twas a good dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T14:59:21-07:00","id":511185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=511029#post511029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Better idea - if you don't know about Changeling, instead of which Seeming &amp; Kith, tell which which of these scares you more:<br /> Fear of the unknown<br /> Fear of turning into a monster<br /> Fear of giving into instincts and losing yourself<br /> Fear of living up to standards you can't meet<br /> Fear of being left behind<br /> Fear of being overwhelmed by something bigger than yourself</div> </div> </div> </div>Fear of being left behind..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T16:49:52-07:00","id":511306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Better idea - if you don't know about Changeling, instead of which Seeming &amp; Kith, tell which which of these scares you more:<br /> Fear of the unknown<br /> Fear of turning into a monster<br /> Fear of giving into instincts and losing yourself<br /> Fear of living up to standards you can't meet<br /> Fear of being left behind<br /> Fear of being overwhelmed by something bigger than yourself</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind if I give it a shot? (If you do, ignore what's in the spoiler)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When faced with an obstacle, what is your immediate, if not rational, reaction?</div> </div> </div> </div>For a true obstacle? Frustration. &quot;Oh man, this is gonna take forever.&quot; Also procrastination, depending on the nature of said obstacle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you did get taken, what do you think you'd miss the most?</div> </div> </div> </div>My family; I wouldn't know what had happened to them or whether or not they knew I was still alive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many dreams do you remember? Do you remember more good or bad?</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember my dreams sometimes. I think it leans more towards the bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better idea - if you don't know about Changeling, instead of which Seeming &amp; Kith, tell which which of these scares you more:</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see... the one thing I'm afraid of the most is that I'll never turn out to be the person I should be, so...<br /> <br /> Fear of living up to standards you can't meet is the closest? I think?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 05-11-2015, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T06:34:31-07:00","id":511960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=511029#post511029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better idea - if you don't know about Changeling, instead of which Seeming &amp; Kith, tell which which of these scares you more:<br /> Fear of the unknown<br /> Fear of turning into a monster<br /> Fear of giving into instincts and losing yourself<br /> Fear of living up to standards you can't meet<br /> Fear of being left behind<br /> Fear of being overwhelmed by something bigger than yourself</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing i most fear is not being able to defeat my defects, thus evolving into a bitter mockery of myself. So,among your answers, i think the closest one is &quot;Fear of living up to standards you can't meet&quot;. The thing is, in my fear there's also parts of that &quot;fear of turning into a monster&quot;,and fear of &quot;being overwhelmed&quot;... but by myself. <br /> <br /> Speaking of impacient, you don't need to worry at all. As far as i'm concerned, you're being really nice (you all, in fact, taking into account my sudden intromission in your thread) spending your time in creating our changeling-selves and considering our answers, so... take all the time you want. And thank you in advance! <br /> <br /> If you need more answers, don't hesitate to fire more questions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T07:26:22-07:00","id":511983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=511069#post511069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not aimed at me, but I have definite stress and fear about living up to standards I can't meet and being overwhelmed by things bigger than me. You've seen my freakouts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arc, buddy, I've tried and tried, but I keep coming back to the same thing - Elemental Air/Lightning. The actual purpose might shift, but everything I've dreamed up for you ends the same. Someone wants that spark and energy and to harness it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 05-12-2015, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T07:55:48-07:00","id":511991,"title":"","content":"Hey, I can dig it. I love a good storm cloud, and the elemental discord between air, water, and fire does fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:35:22-07:00","id":512055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=509270#post509270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, thank you for the welcoming and the poetry! Second, excuse my mistakes writing english. Third... here we go with the answers:<br /> <br /> My answer depends on what kind of obstacle it is:<br /> - If i think (even at instinctual level) that i can solve it, after a flash of frustration i go into it and try to solve it by the most logical way i can think of.<br /> - If i feel i cannot do anything about it, or maybe that is unfair, i usually rage... and then there's a little pause while i try to fight my own anger.<br /> <br /> I'm seriously not sure about that. I think that i would arrive to the kind of situation that makes you to be surprised by the thing/person you're actually missing. Anyway, right now i'd say my hated/loved soon-to-be ex-girlfriend.<br /> <br /> I half remember lots of dreams. The ones i remember clearly are usually of two types: the terrific ones, or those in which i'm flying. Lately i'm having more of the bad stuff.<br /> <br /> As i said, i couldn't tell, i'm noobish in Changeling stuff. I could tell you what Vampire Clan my friends were thinking for me, though, if it is of any help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh wait, do i have to answer also the tie breaker question too? Just in case, here it is:<br /> <br /> They definitely could offer something tempting enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here you go....<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The deal was simple and straight forward \u2013 end the pain of loss. You\u2019re tired of hurting, tired of being sad, tired of the pain. The Keeper was beautiful and lyrical in voice and made it all very easy. And she took away the pain, and the emotions, and the form. She molded you into exactly what she needed and nothing else. A nice little dolly to play with. Put back on the shelf when playtime was over. Taken out when the whim hit. Her favorite plaything for who the hell knows how long. And it all worked out\u2026.until she got bored with her and got a new plaything. You were left on the shelf longer and longer. You collected dust. You didn\u2019t realize that she had screwed up until caked in dust\u2026.she hadn\u2019t quite removed ALL your humanity. There was a sliver left. It had been satisfied by being a favorite toy for so long, but now it was burning like a fire in your wooden body. Eventually, that fire was enough motivation to let you get up off the shelf and walk thru the door of the giant dollhouse you\u2019ve been living in all this time. You\u2019ve returned to the world an Elemental Manikin, a being of wood and little doweled joints.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:38:35-07:00","id":512058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=511991#post511991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I can dig it. I love a good storm cloud, and the elemental discord between air, water, and fire does fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was one of them....becoming part of a storm cloud. Also a gas light statue converted to electrical in a Victorian era realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T10:10:49-07:00","id":512103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=509870#post509870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, I'm sober and not naked. Let's answer some questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Cold/Hot fury. I know. Not a sexy answer, but I literally yelled &quot;What the fuck are YOU looking at? Never seen a fat guy smoking a fucking cigarette?? Come on over, motherfucker. Come on!!&quot; yesterday. Turned out he's my new neighbor and he was just wondering who I was, just pacing my yard and smoking.<br /> <br /> 2. I'd probably miss my friends the most. Kinda bald response, but true.<br /> <br /> 3. I remember MOST of my dreams vividly, even years later. They've been, with one notable exception, absolutely terrifying since I was very small.<br /> <br /> 4. Seeming probably (I play as much CtL as I juggle chainsaws) and just so I can self-label, I'd probably turn out to be Ogre, Elemental or Bestial. Feel free to question any and all of my answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind, Az, I probably know a little better how you think of yourself, and used that in here.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You\u2019re imp like Keeper thought he found a gold mine in you. He was into all things dangerous and a bit crazy to deal with. He was like Steve Irwin, but without having to fear anything he pulled into his world. He took everything he saw in yourself and twisted it into coils and fangs and scales and made you the biggest, bas ass snake he could make of you and then he shoved you under the front porch of his house to hunt the rats you found underneath. While that was okay for sustenance, you were not happy with the circumstances, so you made lunges at him every time he came out of his home\u2026.and he seemed to love it. It\u2019s as if he got you JUST because he knew you\u2019d lash out at him. That\u2019s what he wanted. He was never mad about it, though you always took one hell of a beating as he chased you back under the porch. After this routine for what seemed like weeks, you saw the imp pack up a cart and roll off into the distance. Already tired of this mess, you started slithering for the bushes he yanked you thru originally. The more you slithered, the harder it got, until you noticed you had legs to use again. Legs led to skittering which led to running which led to the end of the Hedges. You\u2019ve come out a Beast Coldscale, kin to all things reptilian, but with a special affinity for large snakes.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T10:21:42-07:00","id":512109,"title":"","content":"Well, this is fun. Maybe when you finish with everyone else I may try the questionaire myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T14:15:57-07:00","id":512331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=512055#post512055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here you go....<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The deal was simple and straight forward \u2013 end the pain of loss. You\u2019re tired of hurting, tired of being sad, tired of the pain. The Keeper was beautiful and lyrical in voice and made it all very easy. And she took away the pain, and the emotions, and the form. She molded you into exactly what she needed and nothing else. A nice little dolly to play with. Put back on the shelf when playtime was over. Taken out when the whim hit. Her favorite plaything for who the hell knows how long. And it all worked out\u2026.until she got bored with her and got a new plaything. You were left on the shelf longer and longer. You collected dust. You didn\u2019t realize that she had screwed up until caked in dust\u2026.she hadn\u2019t quite removed ALL your humanity. There was a sliver left. It had been satisfied by being a favorite toy for so long, but now it was burning like a fire in your wooden body. Eventually, that fire was enough motivation to let you get up off the shelf and walk thru the door of the giant dollhouse you\u2019ve been living in all this time. You\u2019ve returned to the world an Elemental Manikin, a being of wood and little doweled joints.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Delightful. Thank you for your insight and the story, Papa Bear, love it in every aspect. I have one question, though: why do you envision my Changeling-self as wooden? That was an intriguing point!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":1349,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","user":"Phersus","date":".  Those misspelled words, tho XD 05-12-2015, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T14:56:19-07:00","id":512350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=512331#post512331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Delightful. Thank you for your insight and the story, Papa Bear, love it in every aspect. I have one question, though: why do you envision my Changeling-self as wooden? That was an intriguing point!</div> </div> </div> </div>One part inspiration from the Changeling corebook, one part from the answers you gave indicated a greater transformation to non-human would be appropriate, one part tradition (wooden dolls).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T08:02:31-07:00","id":512916,"title":"","content":"Nice explanation and sharp eye, and nicer story still. Thank you again, P.Bear <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T07:49:44-07:00","id":518005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=510090#post510090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mind if I answer these as well? This looks like a fun and interesting game.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1/Try to find a loophole, or the easy path. If I can, cheat my way around it.<br /> <br /> 2/I guess... my friends. At least some of them, which does sound cheesy, yes.<br /> <br /> 3/Only a few, and I mostly remember them for a few hours after I'm awake. Neither good or bad, but mostly weird, although some are fun.<br /> <br /> 4/Either Beast and Broadback, or Elemental and Woodblood. Or maybe Earthbones. It mostly depends if we're talking about the Kith/Seeming I'd like to be because of my interests, or the form which my Keeper would give me.<br /> <br /> And just in case, here is the tiebreaker question :<br /> <br /> <i>If a Keeper were to take you, how would they do it? Could they make a tempting enough offer? Would it be kicking &amp; screaming?</i><br /> <br /> Sadly, yes, I could definitely be tempted. Show me wonders and pleasures, offer me easy and peaceful solutions to my problems, and even if I might suspect a trap, I'll follow my Keeper.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...And now I just realized that most of my answers are depressing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't want you to think I forgot about you. Just stuck at a crossroads. I keep coming back to Darkling, but not sure which Kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T12:05:35-07:00","id":518358,"title":"","content":"Oh, I don't mind. I kinda forced my way in, honestly, so I can't complain. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Although, Darkling? Of all six seemings, I must say that's the one I expected the least. Interesting choice, though.<br /> <br /> Feel free to ask more questions if it can help, I'll be glad to answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T12:17:33-07:00","id":518370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=511029#post511029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Better idea - if you don't know about Changeling, instead of which Seeming &amp; Kith, tell which which of these scares you more:<br /> Fear of the unknown<br /> Fear of turning into a monster<br /> Fear of giving into instincts and losing yourself<br /> Fear of living up to standards you can't meet<br /> Fear of being left behind<br /> Fear of being overwhelmed by something bigger than yourself</div> </div> </div> </div>what if you experience all of those so often and so intensely you can't pick one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T17:21:56-07:00","id":518603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=518370#post518370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what if you experience all of those so often and so intensely you can't pick one?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you answer the other questions, I might still be able to narrow something down for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T17:45:52-07:00","id":518613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=499699#post499699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few questions first:<br /> <br /> When faced with an obstacle, what is your immediate, if not rational, reaction?<br /> <br /> If you did get taken, what do you think you'd miss the most?<br /> <br /> How many dreams do you remember? Do you remember more good or bad?<br /> <br /> Which one do YOU think you'd be? Don't explain why, just give Seeming and Kith.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Keep in mind I know nothing about changeling<br /> <br /> 1. It really depends. Sometimes I have a panic attack, other times I can handle it calmly. If I'm already basically in a working frenzy, I'll just try to work harder and faster until its done (this has almost gotten me hurt a couple of times)<br /> 2. Music. Definitely music. And anime, and video games.<br /> 3. A lot. Mostly bad. I can still remember a nightmare I must have had around the age of 3 or 4. <br /> 4. no clue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T19:42:29-07:00","id":518713,"title":"","content":"Random question: what's it called when a hitter splits a baseball open while at bat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T08:05:23-07:00","id":519585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=518713#post518713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random question: what's it called when a hitter splits a baseball open while at bat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Last time I heard about anyone doing that, the commentator said something about &quot;knocking the hide off it&quot;. Not sure if there's any other term. I think it's too rare an event to get a regularly used term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T09:23:45-07:00","id":519684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=518358#post518358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I don't mind. I kinda forced my way in, honestly, so I can't complain. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Although, Darkling? Of all six seemings, I must say that's the one I expected the least. Interesting choice, though.<br /> <br /> Feel free to ask more questions if it can help, I'll be glad to answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Took a bit, but the inspiration finally hit.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It was the trees that first got your attention. Tall, majestic, beautiful lights coming thru the canopy. You\u2019d wandered thru a fascinating arch just before sundown\u2026.or at least that\u2019s what you told yourself as to why it suddenly got so dark. Trying to find your way back, you suddenly found yourself caught in some low branches that simply would not let go. Next thing you know, you\u2019ve been lifted off the ground. The tree is speaking to you. It says you belong to it now, and it needs you. There are a thousand little bugging things flitting and jumping thru his branches and those of this children. He tasks you with catching and eating them. He twists and contorts your body in that dark forest, ripping you down to smaller pieces and creating a scuttling, winged thing that can catch everything in the forest. In that blackness, you hunt for him thru all four seasons, how many times they rotated thru, you\u2019re not sure anymore. Years of hiding and hunting in the dark has made your eyes super-sensitive to the light, which is how you spotted it. The arch is full of blinding sunlight. You suddenly make a swift lunge for it, letting your wings thrust you as fast as possible. As you move, the branches claw and scratch at you, ripping some things away and, oddly, returning some pieces. By the time you reach the arch, the wings are too small to be useful but you have legs to run. You dive thru the arch and away from the clawing branches, which wither and die as they cross the arch. You\u2019ve returned to the world decades later as a creature of darkness and gliding in silence, a Darkling Lurkglider, skilled in the hunt from above and from the shadows.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T10:46:52-07:00","id":519755,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I quite like this little backstory, even if I'm really surprised by the choice of a Darkling, which I usually automatically avoid at character creation. Although the Lurkgliders might be one of the very few kiths of this seeming that I don't find unsettling. <br /> <br /> Did you aim for a form that would be my opposite, inflicted by an especially cruel Keeper?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T12:06:10-07:00","id":519829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=519755#post519755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you aim for a form that would be my opposite, inflicted by an especially cruel Keeper?</div> </div> </div> </div>A little bit of that is involved, yes. I try to strike a balance between what your answers indicate and what a Keeper might do, and sometimes they're nice and sometimes they're not. A Gentry only has so much to work with, but I've only got those few questions to go on, so I think it comes out more interesting that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T12:17:34-07:00","id":519835,"title":"","content":"Well, that would certainly makes me a pretty miserable Changeling, who'd surely go for the Winter court.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the interesting story, again!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T08:26:45-07:00","id":523269,"title":"","content":"EXPANSION/EXPLANATION:<br /> I feel like tossing this out, not only to show how I\u2019m coming up with these things, but just generally to discuss it and because I want to share.<br /> To me, Changeling: the Lost is the most terrifying game White Wolf/Onyx Path has ever produced. It hits me on a primal, visceral level that the others can\u2019t match. I\u2019ve never even played it, just read the books. There\u2019s several reasons for that, and I\u2019ll go into a few here. <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>More so than the other games, as a Changeling, your life is taken from you. It\u2019s not as simple as a transformation into a vampire or a werewolf where you have to give up that life or adjust it. A mage can continue in that former life for some time. A Promethean, unless they manage to keep their former memories, is essentially dead and has to start over. But a Changeling\u2026..they get taken someplace else, removed entirely from the situation and left to deal with that for the entire Durance. Then, upon their return, they could find no one noticed (which hurts a lot), they\u2019ve had a Fetch destroying their lives (which hurts a lot), a Fetch has been doing a better job of being them than they ever did (which hurts a lot), having missed out on years of their life (which hurts a lot), or (if it\u2019s been a really long Durance) no life at all to return to (which hurts a lot). And then there\u2019s always a chance you\u2019ll be dragged RIGHT BACK INTO IT.</li> <li>While they are all fantasy, it\u2019s more \u201crealistic\u201d in the sense that one can be abducted, abused and returned to their life very changed. It\u2019s a common occurrence with rape victims, kidnapping victims, soldiers, police, etc. There\u2019s a whole disorder for it, PTSD.</li> <li>What you can become is what you fear. While each of the splats can be scary and represent something, both actually and metaphorically, that is feared, to me the Seemings take this to another level by manifesting as common human fears. The Beast is the fear of struggling for life, the Darkling is the fear of the unknown, the Elemental is the fear of losing control and being overwhelmed, the Fairest is the fear of being held to such expectations that you can never attain them, the Ogre is the fear of becoming the monster in the attempt to beat it, the Wizened is the fear of being left behind and/or forgotten. The Gentry works with what is within the character, so those fears are what is most likely to come out.</li> <li>We have different names for dreams and nightmares because we want them to be different things, but in reality a dream is a dream is a dream and they all come from the same place. That part of our heads that can give us wonderful dreams can also give us horrible nightmares. They have to go together, so it\u2019s always going to be terrific and horrific and beautiful at the same time. Again, the other may have the potential for these things, too, but it\u2019s so built into Changeling that there\u2019s no getting around it.</li> <li>I think those of us with mental problems can see the dilemma in Clarity a bit better than others. It\u2019s real easy to get lost inside your own perceptions to the point of losing touch with reality.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T12:19:03-07:00","id":524619,"title":"","content":"Nice explanation and beautiful description before it. Just s you know, i'm stalking this thread now P.Bear and everyone else. Is odd (in a good sense) the feeling of knowledge and proximity that gives reading about your feelings and ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T12:59:01-07:00","id":524675,"title":"","content":"You know what? I just made some dubious decisions today that would actually confirm my Darkling Seeming. I'm still not afraid of the unknown (or at least, it's really not my biggest fear, it would be the Elemental's or Fairest's), but now I can easily envision it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},