s/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T13:03:08-07:00","id":649242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=642844#post642844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fine, if you want to do things the easy way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I only do everything the easy way. You know that. Except the hard stuff. Make that harder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T11:10:28-07:00","id":906565,"title":"","content":"Today is Hug an Atheist Day, so go find your friendly neighborhood atheist and give them a hug to let them know that you don't care what they believe, you love them anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T12:58:46-07:00","id":906652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=906565#post906565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today is Hug an Atheist Day, so go find your friendly neighborhood atheist and give them a hug to let them know that you don't care what they believe, you love them anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an atheist, I appreciate this post.<br /> <br /> I just finished reading through this whole thread for the first time: I'm glad to read your rantings/ramblings, and I'm glad you ended up with a decent job. I hope that's still a thing. My spouse will find out by the end of the day whether or not she'll be laid off, which is stressful. At least our apartment is clean, so we can start hosting games again. Which I need to find time to do: I've been so weirdly unsatisfied with my gaming recently. I just want either a Storyteller who really enjoys the Chronicles of Darkness system stuff or players who really enjoy the CofD system stuff.<br /> <br /> Or just tell me what kind of scenes they want to happen. I'd love it if more than half of them gave me ideas for downtime scenes that brought in their Touchstones/Aspirations/Vices/Virtues/Merits in some way. I get that as a Storyteller I'm supposed to do a lot, but my players are bad at proactively contributing to the experience -- I mostly have to create an obstacle or scenario for them to overcome. Which sometimes is awesome: my werewolf players threw a frat-/sorority party as <i>gathra</i> for a Spirit of Family and Friendship, while making sure it never got out-of-hand because they're trying to starve a Spirit of Violent Revolution that's trying to take over the Family Spirits' territory. It was great, but it didn't really key into any of the characters' natures or ongoing storylines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T11:25:50-07:00","id":909312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=906652#post906652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As an atheist, I appreciate this post.<br /> <br /> I just finished reading through this whole thread for the first time: I'm glad to read your rantings/ramblings, and I'm glad you ended up with a decent job. I hope that's still a thing. My spouse will find out by the end of the day whether or not she'll be laid off, which is stressful. At least our apartment is clean, so we can start hosting games again. Which I need to find time to do: I've been so weirdly unsatisfied with my gaming recently. I just want either a Storyteller who really enjoys the Chronicles of Darkness system stuff or players who really enjoy the CofD system stuff.<br /> <br /> Or just tell me what kind of scenes they want to happen. I'd love it if more than half of them gave me ideas for downtime scenes that brought in their Touchstones/Aspirations/Vices/Virtues/Merits in some way. I get that as a Storyteller I'm supposed to do a lot, but my players are bad at proactively contributing to the experience -- I mostly have to create an obstacle or scenario for them to overcome. Which sometimes is awesome: my werewolf players threw a frat-/sorority party as <i>gathra</i> for a Spirit of Family and Friendship, while making sure it never got out-of-hand because they're trying to starve a Spirit of Violent Revolution that's trying to take over the Family Spirits' territory. It was great, but it didn't really key into any of the characters' natures or ongoing storylines.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome, and thanks for appreciating my equivalent of Twitter. I could never use that because I have trouble keeping within the character limits.<br /> <br /> Hope your spouse is still employed, but if they're doing lay offs, probably not a stable place to be, anyway.<br /> <br /> And I'm totally with you about players not giving you enough to work with. I've had players like that and I've had the ones that almost give too much. I'll take the too much players any day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T11:32:16-07:00","id":909319,"title":"","content":"Thought of the day:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That is all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T14:53:54-07:00","id":910335,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Thought(s) of the day, Epicurean Philosophy:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">God either wants to eliminate bad things and cannot, or can but does not want to, or neither wishes to nor can, or both wants to and can. If he wants to and cannot, then he is weak \u2013 and this does not apply to god. If he can but does not want to, then he is spiteful \u2013 which is equally foreign to god's nature. If he neither wants to nor can, he is both weak and spiteful, and so not a god. If he wants to and can, which is the only thing fitting for a god, where then do bad things come from? Or why does he not eliminate them?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Don't fear god,</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Don't worry about death;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">What is good is easy to get, and</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">What is terrible is easy to endure.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 06-08-2016, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T11:27:55-07:00","id":910984,"title":"","content":"Thought of the day:<br /> <br /> Have you ever stopped to contemplate the complexity of an automobile?<br /> <br /> A simple 12 volt battery makes a spark between two tiny pieces of metal which ignites the fuel causing the pistons to move about turning a shaft to make the wheels go. So much power from such a tiny start.<br /> <br /> But if that STUPID LITTLE BATTERY dies on you, the entire machine is A USELESS HUNK OF JUNK!!!!<br /> <br /> Not a good start to my morning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T15:59:53-07:00","id":911946,"title":"","content":"Thought of the day:<br /> <br /> Some people will always be assholes. It doesn't matter if they're having a bad day or not. Even on good days, they will still be assholes. No matter how much you try to understand them, they will still be assholes. No matter how much you care for them and try to see past it, they will still be assholes. no matter how kindly you treat them and how much you tell them that their behavior is offensive,<b> THEY WILL STILL BE ASSHOLES</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"use