":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T00:14:39-07:00","id":930220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/190691-the-rambling-rumble-part-2?p=929849#post929849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thought of the day:<br /> <br /> I deal with this person and every time she's here, she's rude and negative. She's also sick a lot, which is why I have to deal with her all the time. At some point, do you think it occurs to her that being a big ball of negativity MIGHT be related to why she's always sick?</div> </div> </div> </div>Life works in spirals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T10:02:08-07:00","id":930917,"title":"","content":"Thought of the day:<br /> <br /> While this is clearly not a perfect analogy and there are other circumstances to be accounted for, there is still some truth to it.<br /> <br /> The other day, someone posted a meme-style pic about how working for a wage that does not allow one to support themselves is just a few steps away from slavery. That's not what I'm arguing, though. If considered a bit, it seems slavery could be a better choice.<br /> <br /> I look around at how much time, effort and money put into some of the expensive things they own, like cars, homes, luxury items, etc. As a slave, you are not a cheap commodity. You're an investment. As such, they would have to feed you sufficiently to stay healthy, clothe you appropriately for the environment, house you well enough to stay healthy and safe, see to your health care so that you can continue to work, and (potentially depending on the laws governing ownership) since you've never done anything else with your life they could have to tend to you in your old age (don't roll your eyes, they used to do it all the time). As a slave, you don't own anything, so there is no mortgage, no car payments, no big ticket items, no depressing crush of seeing your back account empty almost as fast as it fills. Granted, yes, you may have to take a few lashings of the skin. But are those really that awful compared to the lashing of the spirit working the daily grind for what amounts to nothing creates? That's up to you to decide.<br /> <br /> How sad is it that living in Middle Class America can actually look like a <b>less </b>preferable situation than being a slave? Personally, I could never do it, but I think I have <a href=\"http://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/oppositional-defiant-disorder/basics/definition/con-20024559\" target=\"_blank\">ODD</a>, so defying authority is practically a reflex action for me. I'd be beat to death inside of a month. But, hey, not a lot of worries left in that state of existence, either. Worrying is for the living.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T10:01:22-07:00","id":934555,"title":"","content":"Thought of the day:<br /> <br /> <b>I AM SO SICK TO DEATH OF BINARY THINKING!!!!!!!!!</b><br /> <br /> Why the hell do so many people so easily fall into this line of thinking? Either you want abortion doctors <i>dead </i>or you're okay with <b>3rd </b>trimester abortions. Either you want all the (insert horrid slur here) <i>dead</i>, or you're a hippie-commie-junkie <b>burden </b>on &quot;the system&quot;. Either you want everybody to have automatic weapons and <i>shoot </i>at each other like it's the Old West or you want every firearm in the <b>world </b>melted down to make Nobel Peace Prizes.<br /> <br /> <b>THERE ARE DEGREES TO EVERYTHING AND IT'S NOT &quot;<i>FENCE SITTING</i>&quot; IF I DON'T CHOOSE A SIDE! THE <i>WRONG THINKING </i>IS THAT THERE ARE <i>ONLY TWO SIDES</i>!!!</b><br /> <br /> Sheesh. Humans are the only know intelligent life in the universe and so many don't act like it.<br /> <br /> Today, I am happy to be a bear.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">((can you tell the current political cycle is getting on my bad side?))</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 07-20-2016, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","na